-- title:
--   Original source two stopped grid limits imply the complete finite-horizon Avram HJB dividend expectation bound
-- statement:
--   A source-complete controlled Ito-Meyer assembly consequence for the exact original spectrally negative Levy process and admissible dividend strategy. Starting from the Proved original clipped four-event grid and assuming two separately specified genuine source/discount and full Stieltjes dividend mesh limits, the assembled almost-sure stopped Ito identity follows. Under the generator inequality and dividend-gradient floor, BV C1 or UBV C2 regularity, w(0)>=0, original right-continuous stopped clock bounded by ruin and finite T, the accepted expectation theorem then establishes E[Term+Cash]<=w(x), E[Cash]<=w(x) and the exact ENNReal complete discounted dividend expectation bound. Genuine source martingale centring, component integrability and nonpositive finite variation remain explicit hypotheses.
-- source:
--   Avram Prop.4(i) Eq. (5.11)-(5.13). Direct composition of Proved e92-derived 2983886e two-limit chain rule and Proved dbc39b9f source-inequality stopped expected budget.

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_AvramDividend_Classical_SpectrallyNegativeLevy
import Definitions.Def_AvramDividend_Classical_DividendStrategy
import Theorems.Thm_AvramDividend_Classical_avram_wave6_06_original_ruin_grid_two_component_limit_assembles_ito
import Theorems.Thm_AvramDividend_Classical_avram_wave6_06_original_source_inequality_hjb_stopped_expected_budget_conditional_ito

open MeasureTheory Set Filter Topology
